---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { NAV } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="Install as a Mobile or Desktop PWA"
  description="Install Itemized on iOS, Android, or desktop as a Progressive Web App for fast shopping list checks and live barcode scanning."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Install</p>
      <h1>Use Itemized like a native app on every device.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Itemized is an installable Progressive Web App (PWA). Add it straight from your browser—no app store account required.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="https-prereq-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 id="https-prereq-title">Before you install: serve over HTTPS</h2>
      <div class="callout callout-warn">
        <p>
          <strong>HTTPS is required for mobile camera barcode scanning.</strong> iOS Safari and mobile browsers on iOS and Android disable <code>navigator.mediaDevices</code> on plain <code>http://</code> LAN addresses.
        </p>
        <p>
          Put Itemized behind a reverse proxy (Nginx Proxy Manager, Caddy, Traefik, SWAG, or Tailscale Serve) before adding it to your home screen. <a href={`${NAV.selfHost}#https`}>See the HTTPS reverse proxy guide →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="platforms-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Step by step</p>
        <h2 id="platforms-title">Add Itemized to your home screen</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="smartphone" size={20} /></div>
          <h3>iOS (Safari)</h3>
          <p>
            1. Open your HTTPS Itemized URL in Safari.<br />
            2. Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button in the toolbar.<br />
            3. Choose <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong> and tap <strong>Add</strong>.<br />
            4. Launch Itemized full-screen from your home screen.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="smartphone" size={20} /></div>
          <h3>Android (Chrome)</h3>
          <p>
            1. Open your HTTPS Itemized URL in Chrome.<br />
            2. Tap the browser menu (three dots) or the install prompt.<br />
            3. Tap <strong>Add to Home screen</strong> → <strong>Install</strong>.<br />
            4. Launch Itemized from your app drawer or home screen.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="server" size={20} /></div>
          <h3>Desktop (Chrome / Edge)</h3>
          <p>
            1. Open your Itemized URL in Chrome, Edge, or Brave.<br />
            2. Click the <strong>Install</strong> icon in the address bar.<br />
            3. Confirm to run Itemized in its own dedicated window with full keyboard shortcuts.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scanners-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Hardware scanners</p>
      <h2 id="scanners-title">USB and Bluetooth barcode scanners</h2>
      <p>
        In addition to your phone’s camera, Itemized works directly with standard keyboard-wedge <strong>USB</strong> and <strong>Bluetooth</strong> barcode scanners in the unified <strong>Scan / Action</strong> workflow.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Plug in a USB scanner at a desktop or kitchen terminal, open <strong>Scan / Action</strong> (shortcut <kbd>g</kbd> <kbd>o</kbd>), and scan items continuously to Purchase, Consume, Open, Transfer, or Audit a location.</li>
        <li>Pair a pocket Bluetooth scanner with a phone or tablet for fast chest-freezer or pantry audits without holding up the camera.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${NAV.selfHost}#https`}>
          <span>Set up HTTPS reverse proxy</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={NAV.features}>Explore all features</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
